WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
John: Happy Project for Awesome!
Hank: Woo!!
John: Ba-ohh

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.100
Hank: That was disappointing.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.220
John: Don’t worry. I’ve got more, Hank. I’ve got more confetti!

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:09.720
Hank: A little one.
John: Pa-pow!

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.680
Oh, it’s the most magical time of the year.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.840
Phil: The only way to go from here is down.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:18.180
Ettore: I’m one of many Save the Children
employees here, and we have a final parting message.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.460
Stand by for that.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:21.960
Save the Children Staff: Don’t forget to
be awesome!

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.000
Emily: This isn’t—this isn’t my first
rodeo on the Project for Awesome livestream.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.360
Sherrie: Doesn’t he look beautiful today?

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.980
Big Bird: We all could stand to be a little
kinder, don’t you think?

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.060
Sherrie: Project for Awesome is such an awesome
idea—

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.220
Big Bird: Oh, don’t forget to be awesome!
Sherrie: Exactly!

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.900
Hank: Take a screenshot. It’ll last longer.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.180
Lindsey: Oh my gosh, it’s so cold!

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:44.200
John: People are calling me Glitter Beard—oh,
it’s ‘cause you want me to put glitter in my beard.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.000
Rhett: Once you fall in love with the em dash—good, woah, buddy—
Link: Good woah buddy

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.780
We've already passed $315,000! What!

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:51.960
Hank: How are we all going to die, Phil?

00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:53.480
Pat: You’re not better than Times New Roman.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.129
Grace &amp; Mamrie: 1, 2, 3 candle!

00:00:55.129 --> 00:00:56.749
OHHH MY GOD!!!

00:00:56.749 --> 00:00:58.180
Grace: Prove Hank wrong!

00:00:58.180 --> 00:00:59.040
Grace, Mamrie, and Hannah: Prove Hank wrong!

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.319
Hank: Well, John just arrived in the chat,
so now everybody’s really excited, and—

00:01:02.319 --> 00:01:04.139
Gabby: Wait, you know John Green?

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:09.500
Nathan (Obama): We’re gonna be here in Trump’s
America, we gotta do a couple things.

00:01:09.509 --> 00:01:16.589
Sabrina: How does a ragtag volunteer army
in need of a shower somehow defeat a global superpower?

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:18.660
Mamrie: Does it hurt?

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:52.440
Gideon: *sings*

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.440
Hank: Okay, going up on my forehead, Kendall.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.680
My kerning was a little off there, Alex.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.160
Lex: Is everyone happy with their kitty time?

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:02.170
Destin: Josh, you are, you are the McCall.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:03.299
John *reading a question*: So what do you
think of Mars?

00:02:03.299 --> 00:02:05.600
John: I think it is a cold, dead rock in the
middle of the ocean.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.360
Charlie: As many bread demon emojis as you
can in the chat.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:09.360
That will be helpful.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.000
Charlie, Emily, Rosianna: The power of bread
compels you!

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:16.000
John: Oh, Hank, you put up Cheez Doodles Guy!

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.340
John: YAAAAASSS!!!
Hank: YES!

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.380
Team SciShow: Woo!

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:23.900
Hank: And s fantastic Project for Awesome. I’m so proud of this community.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:24.610
I’m back!

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:29.200
Thanks for our fabulous tenth ever Project for Awesome. Had a great time.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.210
My mind is still a little bit hungover from
it.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:32.600
Also, just coming back!

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:35.380
I'm—I’m so glad that that’s how I
came back.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:41.040
To the Project for Awesome, to Nerdfighteria
working together to raise over two million dollars.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.500
It’s still going on, by the way, if you
wanna get one of those last-minute perks,

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:48.740
if you watch this within the first twelve
hours of it being up, you can go to projectforawesome.com/donate

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:49.830
and get some stuff.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:53.700
Obviously thanks to everybody who helped make
this happen, everybody who donated, everybody

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:57.820
who shared it, everybody who voted on videos,
everybody who made videos, all of the volunteers

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:00.160
who put it all together, all of the people
who joined us in the livestream.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.190
Going away for the last six weeks has been
really weird.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:06.190
I’ve never done it before, never left this
channel in almost ten years of making videos.

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:07.930
And it was a really weird time to do that.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:11.800
I’m really used to, like, when something
in the world is going on that I want to talk about,

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:15.560
just talking about it, and it was interesting
to take a break from that during a moment

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:18.840
in which everyone really wanted to say some
things.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:24.420
I think it really changed me, and I’m really
interested to see how that manifests as I

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:27.940
get back into making videos and get a chance
to say some of the things I’ve been thinking about.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:31.880
We got many more larger donations this year,
so I’m gonna thank a bunch of those people in the description.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:35.740
We also got a $25,000 matching donation from
YouTube as part of their new Creators for

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:38.350
Change project, which I will link to in the
description.

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:42.130
Basically, YouTube is reaching out with money
to a bunch of different YouTube creators who

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:44.330
are dealing with social issues on their channels.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:48.530
Creators who are promoting awareness, tolerance,
and empathy with the kind of content that they make.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:49.530
It’s a really cool program.

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:50.430
Link in the description.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.070
John, thanks so much for doing this with me.

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:54.450
Everybody, thank you for your support of the
Project for Awesome.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:58.080
projectforawesome.com/donate if you want to
get those last-minute perks.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:59.810
John, I’ll see you on Monday.

